I wanted to share the final proposed design for the Google Chrome AD group structure and request your review and approval.

The design has been prepared using a layered approach to clearly separate Policy, Deployment, and Access management. The objective is to ensure a cleaner and more controlled deployment model while reducing assignment conflicts and improving long-term manageability.

Key improvements in the proposed structure include:

Single policy assignment source for consistent Chrome configuration

Clear separation between Required and Available deployments

Permission-based access management for controlled eligibility

Elimination of overlapping group assignments

Simplified troubleshooting and operational ownership

Improved scalability for future administration and support

This approach also ensures that Chrome policies are applied only where the application is deployed, helping maintain configuration consistency across the environment.

The document additionally includes:

Logical group nesting structure

End-to-end deployment flow

Access control model

Before vs After comparison for operational clarity

